## 📝 Quick Reference

### Subquery Locations

| Location | Purpose | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `WHERE` | Filter rows | `WHERE price > (SELECT AVG(price) FROM products)` |
| `SELECT` | Value per row | `(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders WHERE customer_id = c.customer_id)` |
| `FROM` | Derived table | `FROM (SELECT city, COUNT(*) FROM customers GROUP BY city) AS t` |
| `HAVING` | Filter groups | `HAVING COUNT(*) > (SELECT AVG(cnt) FROM (...) t)` |

---

### IN vs EXISTS

| | IN | EXISTS |
|---|---|---|
| How it works | Checks value against full list | Checks if any rows returned |
| Stops early | No — checks all values | Yes — stops at first match |
| Speed on large data | Slower | Faster |
| NULL safety | NOT IN has NULL trap | NOT EXISTS is NULL safe |
| Use when | Small subquery list | Large subquery result |

---



### Correlated vs Non-Correlated

```sql
-- Non-correlated — runs ONCE, result reused
WHERE price > (SELECT AVG(price) FROM products)

-- Correlated — runs ONCE PER ROW, references outer query
WHERE price > (
    SELECT AVG(p2.price) FROM products p2
    WHERE p2.category = p1.category  -- ← references outer p1
)
```

---

## ⚠️ Common Mistakes

| Mistake | Fix |
|---|---|
| Forgetting parentheses around subquery | Always wrap in `( )` |
| FROM subquery without alias | Add `AS alias_name` after closing `)` |
| NOT IN with NULLs in subquery | Add `WHERE col IS NOT NULL` or use `NOT EXISTS` |
| Correlated subquery on large tables | Rewrite as JOIN + GROUP BY when possible |
| Subquery returns multiple rows in WHERE = | Use `IN` not `=` when subquery returns multiple rows |

